            {{!-- Projects --}}
            <section id="projects" class="scroll-mt-24">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Projects</h2>
                <p class="mt-3">A <strong>project</strong> groups everything for one website or app, like a Figma file. It holds <strong>pages</strong> (full screens) and each page's <strong>sections</strong> (header, hero, pricing, footer). Open <a href="/projects" class="font-medium underline">Projects</a> in the sidebar.</p>
                <div class="mt-5 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
                    <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4"><p class="font-medium text-gray-900">One plane</p><p class="mt-1 text-sm">Every page and section is a live frame on a single infinite canvas, like Figma. Scroll or drag the background to pan, Ctrl/Cmd + scroll to zoom, <strong>Fit</strong> to see everything. Drag a frame to arrange it (positions are saved), double-click to open it in the editor, <strong>Tidy up</strong> to reset the layout.</p></div>
                    <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4"><p class="font-medium text-gray-900">Add to a project</p><p class="mt-1 text-sm"><strong>+ New page</strong> on the board, the Project box in the save dialog, or the Project dropdown on any Library card.</p></div>
                    <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4"><p class="font-medium text-gray-900">From Claude</p><p class="mt-1 text-sm">Ask: "Design a landing page and a pricing page and save them in a project called Acme website." Claude creates the project and files both pages.</p></div>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-4 text-sm"><strong>Active project and brief.</strong> Press <strong>Set as active</strong> on a project's board to tell Claude "this is what I'm working on". When Claude connects it is told the active project, its <strong>brief</strong> (brand, tone, colors, navigation, rules, written in the panel on the right) and the pages already designed, so new pages match the old ones. Saves go to the active project by default, and you can say "switch to the Mobile app project" or "remember that every page has a top bar" and Claude updates it for you.</p>
                <p class="mt-4 text-sm">Deleting a project never deletes its pages: they go back to your Library. Claude can also list projects and read a project's structure (<code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 font-mono text-[13px]">list_projects</code>, <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 font-mono text-[13px]">get_project</code>), so a later chat can continue where you left off.</p>
            </section>

