                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Set it up (once)</h3>
                <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm">
                    <li>Open <a href="/library" class="font-medium underline">Library</a> and find the <em>Connect your
                            coding agent</em> box.</li>
                    <li>Press <strong>Generate token</strong>. A command appears. <strong>Copy it now</strong>: the
                        token is shown only once (generating a new one cancels the old).</li>
                    <li>Paste the command into your terminal. For Claude Code it looks like this:</li>
                </ol>
                <pre
                    class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-4 font-mono text-[12px] leading-5 text-gray-900">claude mcp add --transport http tailwind-library https://YOUR-SITE/mcp --header "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN"</pre>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm">Then just talk normally, for example: <em>"Build a landing page. Check my
                        component library first and reuse my hero and pricing components."</em></p>

                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">The Connect page and Claude Design</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm">Open <a href="/connect" class="font-medium underline">Connect</a> in the sidebar. It gives you a <strong>Claude Code kit</strong> (project config, a short <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 font-mono text-[13px]">CLAUDE.md</code> section and a skill) and a <strong>design pack</strong> for Claude Design: your design guide, every component with its spec, and a brief to attach.</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm"><strong>Claude on the web:</strong> on the Connect page, copy the connector address into Claude (<em>Settings, Connectors, Add custom connector</em>). You approve access once on a page of this site, and there is no token to copy. You can disconnect any app from the same page. This needs the site to be reachable on the internet over HTTPS.</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm"><strong>The bridge:</strong> design with the pack attached, then bring the result back. If Claude is connected to your library it can save the design itself with <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 font-mono text-[13px]">save_design</code> (one component per screen). Otherwise use <strong>Import designs</strong> in Library: drop HTML files or a <strong>.zip</strong>, or paste HTML. With <em>Split pages into sections</em> on, each page is saved whole and also as one component per section (header, hero, pricing, footer). Everything is private and tagged, with its own spec, and Claude Code can build from it over MCP.</p>

                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">How the agent knows what to use</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm">Agents shouldn't read everything. So the app prepares two summaries for them, automatically:</p>
                <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm">
                    <li><strong>Spec card</strong> (one per component): the colors, text sizes, radius and spacing it uses, how it is built, whether it works on mobile and in dark mode, and whether it needs JavaScript. If AI is on, it also gets a one-line <em>summary</em> and <em>use when / avoid when</em>. It updates whenever the code changes. Open it with <strong>Export</strong> then the <strong>Spec</strong> tab.</li>
                    <li><strong>Design guide</strong> (one per library): your most-used colors, fonts and spacing, plus a short index of every component. Open it with the <strong>Design guide</strong> button in Library. You can download it or paste it into a <code class="rounded bg-gray-100 px-1 font-mono text-[13px]">CLAUDE.md</code>.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm">The agent reads the guide first, searches, reads the short cards of a few matches, and only then fetches the full code for the one or two it will use.</p>

                <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">What the agent can do</h3>
                <div class="mt-3 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white">
                    <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
                        <thead class="bg-gray-50 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">
                            <tr>
                                <th class="px-4 py-2.5">Tool</th>
                                <th class="px-4 py-2.5">In plain words</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[13px] text-gray-900">search_components</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">"Find my pricing components." Searches by keyword or tag.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[13px] text-gray-900">get_component</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">"Give me that one as React." Returns the code in HTML, React, Vue
                                    or Svelte.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[13px] text-gray-900">save_component</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">"Save this new component." Added to your library as private.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[13px] text-gray-900">save_pages</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">"Save these three pages." Saves several pages in one go, each as its own separate component inside one project (Overview, Customers, Transactions).</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[13px] text-gray-900">save_design</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">"Save this finished page." Saves it as one private component. Add "and split it into sections" for a long marketing page and each stacked section (header, hero, pricing, footer) is saved too. Dashboards and app screens are never split.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[13px] text-gray-900">list_tags</td>
                                <td class="px-4 py-3">"What tags do I use?" Returns every tag and how many components
                                    have it.</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-4 text-sm"><strong
                        class="text-gray-900">Treat the token like a password.</strong> Anyone who has it can read and
                    add to your library. If it leaks, generate a new one.</div>
            </section>

